<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    PRIVACY MANIFEST. Mandatory for App Store submission since May 2024.

    Written early, while the code is fresh, because the alternative is auditing
    125 files later for API calls nobody remembers making. Every entry below was
    verified by grepping the actual source, not assumed:

      UserDefaults          DeviceReportStore, onboarding completion, Booster pairing
      File timestamps       scan folders, census files, ScanLibraryStore
      Disk space            the capture storage guard and TrainingBudget

    NOTHING IS COLLECTED. This app has no account, no login, no analytics, no
    third-party SDKs. Scans, photographs, depth measurements and models never
    leave the device unless the user sends them to their own computer. That is
    why NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes is empty, and it is a genuinely strong
    position at review rather than a shortcut.

    ONE EXCEPTION, AND IT MUST NOT SHIP. This file used to say there were no
    network calls except to a PC on the user's own Wi-Fi. That stopped being
    true when the over-the-air self-update went in: Sources/Booster/
    SelfUpdateService.swift posts the bundle id, the installed build number
    and the phone's LAN address to a build broker on the internet. It
    collects nothing about the user and it is development-only, compiled in
    only when CI injects an endpoint, but it is still a call off the local
    network and this file is where that gets admitted.

    BEFORE ANY SUBMISSION: strip SelfUpdateService.swift and its section in
    BoosterTabView, then delete this paragraph. The two go together.

    If anything else ever stops being true, this file must change in the same
    commit.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!-- No tracking, no tracking domains. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyTracking</key>
    <false/>
    <key>NSPrivacyTrackingDomains</key>
    <array/>

    <!-- Nothing is collected, so nothing is declared. -->
    <key>NSPrivacyCollectedDataTypes</key>
    <array/>

    <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypes</key>
    <array>
        <!--
            UserDefaults. CA92.1: read and write only within the app's own
            container, never an app group, never shared with anything.
        -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryUserDefaults</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>CA92.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!--
            File timestamps. C617.1: timestamps of files inside the app's own
            container, to sort the scan library newest first and to tell whether
            a census file belongs to the scan beside it.
        -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryFileTimestamp</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>C617.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>

        <!--
            Disk space. E174.1: checked before and during a capture so the app
            can stop cleanly and say so, rather than filling the phone and
            failing to write the scan it just spent three minutes recording.
        -->
        <dict>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPIType</key>
            <string>NSPrivacyAccessedAPICategoryDiskSpace</string>
            <key>NSPrivacyAccessedAPITypeReasons</key>
            <array>
                <string>E174.1</string>
            </array>
        </dict>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
